--- !u!114 &1489488737
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1489488731}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3ff6acaa8b9f1994499dd387e6188532, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Comments: "This demonstrates how to process audio input using AudioSpectrum and
    AudioSample to drive animation behaviors. The AudioSource may be configured using
    an audio file or live device input such as a microphone or line-in, depending
    on your hardware setup.\n\nNOTES: \nAudio reactive behaviors can only react to
    audio signals as they occur and therefore cannot anticipate what will happen
    next. Music syncronized animation can be improved greatly by using a midi file
    for pre-recorded music. See the MidiSetup example for more.\n\nAlso note that
    audio data often has a lot of spillover across frequencies making it difficult
    or impossible to isolate specific sounds. Set the target frequency range and
    min amplitude on each AudioSample to target a specific section of the audio."
  Warning: 
  URLTitle: 
  URL: 
  URL2Title: 
  URL2: 
